Local engine.py patches (2026-10-19): tap jitter tolerance, 350 ms tap window,
distance-based pointer start, fresh subpixel state, and report-rate-independent gain.
GTK source-event intervals optionally drive velocity; lifetime timing stays monotonic.
Multi-finger gestures stay latched until every contact lifts: a trailing finger
cannot move the pointer or start a glide. Two-to-one transitions clear pointer
origin/velocity; duration, cumulative travel, established pointer intent and max
finger count remain unchanged so real two-finger taps still right-click without
reclassifying an earlier pointer movement as a tap.
Local thor_app.py patch (2026-10-21): route keyboard press/release redraws
through an overridable hook; the vendor default still queues the same full draw.
The local adapter uses bounded keycap damage; keyboard input logic is unchanged.
The paint origin is also overridable, retaining the original burn-in calculation
by default. The adapter keeps a stable origin during partial damage and advances
the OLED orbit on full repaints to avoid seams against retained pixels.
Local thor_app.py patch (2026-10-21): ending a held key also uses the same
overridable redraw hook; the vendor default remains a full redraw. This closes
the release/slide-off path that otherwise bypassed adapter keycap damage.
Local system_stats.py patch (2026-10-22): keep the existing signed V×I battery
power sampling and return None for missing voltage/current rather than false 0 W.
The adapter displays cached net battery power without additional polling.
